  RP process: clustering ratio |r_n - 1| decreasing (n >= 4): True;  min r_n = 1.0013 > 0
  non-RP counterpoint (complex transfer spectrum): the
  separated two-point value changes sign 11 times in
  n <= 40 - 'background eclipses': separations where the
  seal's placement amplitude vanishes or flips.
  -> with RP, T is SELF-ADJOINT: real spectrum, monotone
     T^n -> P_1, no eclipses possible: (E-bg) at RP scope
     needs only per-sector simplicity of eigenvalue 1 -
     no spectral gap, no aperiodicity assumption.  The
     time-symmetry of the ledger is itself what guarantees
     the seal can always be placed.

